1
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:19,830
get up!

2
00:00:27,860 --> 00:00:30,780
I don't know Shut it up!

3
00:01:22,700 --> 00:01:29,000
Woah!

4
00:01:34,380 --> 00:01:35,220
Ah!

5
00:01:41,120 --> 00:01:43,780
It's my dream to explore the world!

6
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:45,360
Sailing far and wide!

7
00:01:46,180 --> 00:01:47,940
Take me with you!

8
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:49,860
We should leave promptly!

9
00:01:50,800 --> 00:01:53,180
You really think we'd go for that?

10
00:01:53,740 --> 00:01:55,211
That's enough out of you.

11
00:01:55,900 --> 00:01:58,420
I've been held back for far too long.

12
00:01:58,700 --> 00:02:01,112
I want to escape this suffocating island.

13
00:02:03,160 --> 00:02:05,440
Please, free me from these chains.

14
00:02:05,700 --> 00:02:09,260
Lord Odin, no. Stop that.
Raise your head. I'm sorry.

15
00:02:09,540 --> 00:02:11,657
Weren't you just trying
to kill our captain?

16
00:02:11,740 --> 00:02:13,520
I beg you. Enough.

17
00:02:13,780 --> 00:02:15,780
This man is a pirate, not an ally.

18
00:02:16,180 --> 00:02:17,560
You're a scourge.

19
00:02:17,720 --> 00:02:20,073
Leave this country before it's too late.

20
00:02:20,860 --> 00:02:23,280
Well, I would leave if I could.

21
00:02:23,700 --> 00:02:27,240
But as you can see, our ship
was damaged on the way here.

22
00:02:27,400 --> 00:02:29,400
So that presents a slight problem.

23
00:02:29,840 --> 00:02:31,075
That won't do at all.

24
00:02:31,240 --> 00:02:32,780
I'll help you repair it!

25
00:02:34,140 --> 00:02:37,860
Listen well, I cannot have you
tempting Lord Odin like this.

26
00:02:38,420 --> 00:02:40,400
Repair the ship quickly and go!

27
00:02:41,860 --> 00:02:43,800
That's exactly my intention.

28
00:02:49,860 --> 00:02:51,097
Stop jogging your feet!

29
00:02:51,180 --> 00:02:52,010
Bring it here!

30
00:02:53,560 --> 00:02:54,390
Hey!

31
00:02:54,520 --> 00:02:56,600
You ready for a snack break? Huh?

32
00:02:56,900 --> 00:02:58,547
We've got some grub for you.

33
00:02:59,620 --> 00:03:00,560
Dig in!

34
00:03:00,760 --> 00:03:01,819
No need to be shy.

35
00:03:03,320 --> 00:03:04,150
Oh!

36
00:03:04,233 --> 00:03:05,460
That looks good!

37
00:03:08,460 --> 00:03:10,520
The flavor of a far-off land!

38
00:03:10,760 --> 00:03:12,700
And what freightel is this?

39
00:03:12,880 --> 00:03:14,840
It's alcohol made from grapes.

40
00:03:15,100 --> 00:03:17,394
So many things out there I need to see.

41
00:03:17,720 --> 00:03:19,200
Show me more!

42
00:03:19,880 --> 00:03:21,120
Take me with you.

43
00:03:21,460 --> 00:03:24,220
I want to solve every mystery in the world

44
00:03:25,240 --> 00:03:27,800
You're not the type to
serve under someone.

45
00:03:27,980 --> 00:03:32,100
I can see it already I can't
just let anyone on my ship.

46
00:03:32,340 --> 00:03:36,516
Do you know what happens when there
are too many selfish people around?

47
00:03:37,420 --> 00:03:39,640
People like you, I mean.

48
00:03:42,680 --> 00:03:44,080
It's too hot.

49
00:03:46,620 --> 00:03:47,880
It's not pretty.

50
00:03:48,260 --> 00:03:51,554
I learned that the hard way
with the last ship I was on.

51
00:03:54,320 --> 00:03:56,440
Why not set sail on your own?

52
00:03:58,300 --> 00:04:03,300
I've tried over and over again, but
every damn time it ends in failure.

53
00:04:03,700 --> 00:04:07,257
I may be strong, but that doesn't
mean I can navigate a ship.

54
00:04:07,340 --> 00:04:10,560
Then give up on sailing and
do whatever your job is.

55
00:04:10,720 --> 00:04:12,777
This country is suffocating me, all right?

56
00:04:12,860 --> 00:04:14,500
I need to be free!

57
00:04:15,580 --> 00:04:16,698
Listen, Whitebeard.

58
00:04:16,820 --> 00:04:20,996
The land of Wano has a law that
strictly bars people from leaving here.

59
00:04:21,460 --> 00:04:23,580
Lord Odin is now the Daimyo of Kaido,

60
00:04:23,780 --> 00:04:26,900
so it would be inexcusable
for him to break that law.

61
00:04:27,120 --> 00:04:29,300
Don't tell him about that! Hmm.

62
00:04:30,320 --> 00:04:31,520
Well, good to know.

63
00:04:31,800 --> 00:04:33,957
Seems you and I are on the same page.

64
00:04:34,040 --> 00:04:36,628
I don't want your Daimyo
on my ship, either.

65
00:04:37,380 --> 00:04:40,320
Do you think I care about
some stuffy old laws?

66
00:04:40,760 --> 00:04:42,317
How insightful of you.

67
00:04:42,400 --> 00:04:45,600
Yes, Lord Odin is
indispensable to our land.

68
00:04:48,480 --> 00:04:50,300
That's enough! You'll be fine!

69
00:04:50,680 --> 00:04:53,200
Take me to Sea Whitebeard! Please!

70
00:04:54,160 --> 00:04:55,020
Help me!

71
00:04:55,480 --> 00:04:57,420
I don't want to be the type, yo!

72
00:04:59,100 --> 00:04:59,930
No!

73
00:05:00,013 --> 00:05:01,160
Please don't make me go home!

74
00:05:01,400 --> 00:05:03,635
This place is suffocating, I tell you!

75
00:05:04,480 --> 00:05:05,820
Untie me, you beasts!

76
00:05:06,160 --> 00:05:07,000
How cruel!

77
00:05:11,040 --> 00:05:13,040
I won't give up!

78
00:05:14,160 --> 00:05:16,660
You cannot stop me!

79
00:05:19,740 --> 00:05:21,380
White beard!

80
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:23,580
Wait for me!

81
00:05:26,520 --> 00:05:29,860
You think there's only
five islands in the world?

82
00:05:31,840 --> 00:05:33,780
Not even close!

83
00:05:34,520 --> 00:05:35,350
What?

84
00:05:35,680 --> 00:05:39,880
Try 10 million, maybe
even 20 million, or more.

85
00:05:41,220 --> 00:05:43,279
Geez, you guys don't know anything.

86
00:05:43,560 --> 00:05:45,440
Sailing the world is a blast.

87
00:05:45,640 --> 00:05:46,800
You should try it.

88
00:05:47,580 --> 00:05:50,020
The world out there is a big place.

89
00:05:50,480 --> 00:05:54,127
There's so many islands, you
could never hope to see them all.

90
00:06:05,360 --> 00:06:06,360
Sneaking off?

91
00:06:08,180 --> 00:06:09,660
Where might you be going?

92
00:06:09,960 --> 00:06:10,790
It's quite late.

93
00:06:10,873 --> 00:06:12,357
You frighten me half to death.

94
00:06:12,440 --> 00:06:13,940
Where are you going?

95
00:06:15,420 --> 00:06:18,257
Does the daimyo need your
permission to take a piss?

96
00:06:18,340 --> 00:06:19,177
Give me a break.

97
00:06:19,260 --> 00:06:20,140
It's nothing.

98
00:06:20,660 --> 00:06:22,072
Do take care, Lord Odin.

99
00:06:22,380 --> 00:06:23,674
The night can be cold.

100
00:06:26,560 --> 00:06:27,390
Ridiculous.

101
00:06:31,320 --> 00:06:34,480
Odin won't be happy we snuck
away at night like this.

102
00:06:36,800 --> 00:06:41,437
A pity, since he was so strong, he
might have been an asset to the crew.

103
00:06:41,520 --> 00:06:46,777
It really seemed like pops liked
him too, I thought he'd say yes!

104
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:49,037
Ah, what are you talking about?

105
00:06:49,120 --> 00:06:50,840
Don't play dumb with us!

106
00:06:56,960 --> 00:06:59,677
Hypothetically, even if I
did take a liking to him,

107
00:06:59,760 --> 00:07:02,197
we still couldn't bring him along with us.

108
00:07:02,280 --> 00:07:04,515
That would be like kidnapping royalty.

109
00:07:06,180 --> 00:07:09,317
Did you leave him that
treasure chest like I told you?

110
00:07:09,400 --> 00:07:12,635
We owe them for all the food
and supplies they gave us.

111
00:07:18,380 --> 00:07:19,720
What the hell is that?

112
00:07:19,880 --> 00:07:23,097
You pirates thought you could
pull one over on me, huh?

113
00:07:23,180 --> 00:07:24,260
Well, too bad!

114
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:27,390
Odin!

115
00:07:27,473 --> 00:07:28,689
Don't let me on that ship!

116
00:07:29,760 --> 00:07:30,937
Not so fast!

117
00:07:31,020 --> 00:07:34,617
I know you think you're clever, my lord,
but you're not getting away that easily.

118
00:07:34,700 --> 00:07:35,940
Now come with me!

119
00:07:38,740 --> 00:07:39,720
That idiot!

120
00:07:40,440 --> 00:07:41,760
Show me the world!

121
00:07:42,180 --> 00:07:44,340
Keep you with you! Why, man?

122
00:07:44,520 --> 00:07:45,780
We need you here!

123
00:07:46,240 --> 00:07:48,300
You're to feed the next Shogun!

124
00:07:48,560 --> 00:07:52,040
Sorry, pal, no means no, but
good luck ruling or whatever.

125
00:07:52,320 --> 00:07:53,900
I'm letting you loose now.

126
00:07:54,160 --> 00:07:55,580
Wait just a moment. Huh?

127
00:07:55,900 --> 00:07:58,997
I'm concerned about the man
who's chasing after Odin.

128
00:07:59,080 --> 00:08:00,139
Bring him up here.

129
00:08:02,320 --> 00:08:03,880
What a pain!

130
00:08:04,840 --> 00:08:06,900
Now, everyone hold on!

131
00:08:07,280 --> 00:08:09,900
Don't worry about those morons from Wano!

132
00:08:10,400 --> 00:08:13,280
We're about to fly over those balls!

133
00:08:25,020 --> 00:08:25,850
No!

134
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:28,577
Lord Odin is gone!

135
00:08:28,660 --> 00:08:31,072
Whitebeard's ship has left the port, too.

136
00:08:31,440 --> 00:08:33,560
My greatest fears are coming true.

137
00:08:35,220 --> 00:08:36,400
Ezo's gone, too.

138
00:08:36,700 --> 00:08:38,229
Even the doggie and kitty.

139
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:39,920
Don't cry, Okiku.

140
00:08:40,540 --> 00:08:43,897
Instead of fearing the worst, we
should search for them as a team.

141
00:08:43,980 --> 00:08:44,840
You with me?

142
00:08:46,400 --> 00:08:47,720
Start the search!

143
00:08:48,180 --> 00:08:49,920
Cover the whole country!

144
00:08:58,660 --> 00:08:59,920
Hey, he's had enough!

145
00:09:00,200 --> 00:09:01,847
You can't let Lord Odin die!

146
00:09:02,080 --> 00:09:03,180
Pull up the chain!

147
00:09:03,480 --> 00:09:04,580
We need him!

148
00:09:04,760 --> 00:09:07,642
The future of our country
rests on his shoulders!

149
00:09:07,820 --> 00:09:08,720
Listen, kid.

150
00:09:08,960 --> 00:09:11,300
You saw me tell him no again and again.

151
00:09:11,940 --> 00:09:15,237
He's the one who turned his
back on that country of yours.

152
00:09:15,320 --> 00:09:19,360
We're on my ship, and that means
we're gonna play by my rules.

153
00:09:23,540 --> 00:09:24,797
Don't do this!

154
00:09:24,880 --> 00:09:26,060
I'm begging you!

155
00:09:26,760 --> 00:09:28,054
That man is dangerous.

156
00:09:28,180 --> 00:09:30,117
I can't let him force his way on board.

157
00:09:30,200 --> 00:09:32,360
I have to protect my family first.

158
00:09:33,500 --> 00:09:36,324
If you want to stop him,
talk him down yourself.

159
00:09:38,680 --> 00:09:39,960
Listen up, Odin.

160
00:09:41,380 --> 00:09:42,460
Three days.

161
00:09:42,980 --> 00:09:46,200
You hang onto that chain for three days.

162
00:09:46,420 --> 00:09:48,185
Then I'll let you come aboard.

163
00:09:51,420 --> 00:09:52,820
Do you swear it?

164
00:09:53,120 --> 00:09:54,120
All your life?

165
00:09:54,940 --> 00:09:55,770
Yeah.

166
00:09:56,060 --> 00:09:57,300
You have my word!

167
00:10:34,760 --> 00:10:36,060
I can't tell.

168
00:10:36,320 --> 00:10:37,496
Is Odin still there?

169
00:10:39,020 --> 00:10:40,560
Uh, yeah, he is.

170
00:10:40,780 --> 00:10:43,060
But he's looking, uh, not great.

171
00:10:43,480 --> 00:10:46,517
Between the waves and everything
else crashed into his face.

172
00:10:46,600 --> 00:10:48,420
He's pretty busted up.

173
00:10:49,820 --> 00:10:52,080
Only one hour left, Odin!

174
00:10:52,340 --> 00:10:54,700
You got this! Let's go!

175
00:10:55,320 --> 00:10:57,849
Hey, you shouldn't be
cheering for the guy.

176
00:10:57,980 --> 00:11:00,357
But Pop said he could join
us if he pulls us off.

177
00:11:00,440 --> 00:11:01,440
Don't you get it?

178
00:11:01,980 --> 00:11:04,300
He's gonna become a member of our crew!

179
00:11:04,980 --> 00:11:05,810
Huh?

180
00:11:07,580 --> 00:11:08,410
Oh?

181
00:11:09,200 --> 00:11:10,900
We'll be your new Gourmet?

182
00:11:14,900 --> 00:11:15,730
Oh!

183
00:11:16,700 --> 00:11:18,280
You can do it!

184
00:11:18,560 --> 00:11:19,740
Just hang on!

185
00:11:20,280 --> 00:11:22,460
Odin! Yeah! Attaboy!

186
00:11:24,700 --> 00:11:25,960
Let's do it, Oda!

187
00:11:27,860 --> 00:11:30,080
Kick him off now! Come on!

188
00:11:30,920 --> 00:11:32,580
Yeah, come on, Oda!

189
00:11:34,080 --> 00:11:35,040
Those fools.

190
00:11:37,600 --> 00:11:39,540
I don't care if it's you, shit.

191
00:11:39,660 --> 00:11:42,297
No one treats my lord like
this and gets away with it.

192
00:11:42,380 --> 00:11:43,498
I'll make you free!

193
00:11:47,660 --> 00:11:49,980
Keep it unloaded! Come on!

194
00:11:50,560 --> 00:11:51,897
I'll do it, Oda!

195
00:11:51,980 --> 00:11:53,237
Almost there, buddy!

196
00:11:53,320 --> 00:11:54,620
Hang on!

197
00:11:55,920 --> 00:11:57,560
Lord Odin, no!

198
00:12:00,140 --> 00:12:00,970
No!

199
00:12:01,140 --> 00:12:02,669
Take your hands off of me!

200
00:12:13,200 --> 00:12:15,060
What a babe!

201
00:12:15,460 --> 00:12:17,340
And she's so classy!

202
00:12:18,860 --> 00:12:20,120
Why are you running?

203
00:12:20,380 --> 00:12:22,397
We'll take you to Wano
just like you asked.

204
00:12:22,480 --> 00:12:25,060
We've got a nice big ship waiting for you.

205
00:12:25,300 --> 00:12:26,917
You don't have to be scared.

206
00:12:27,000 --> 00:12:28,500
We won't hurt you.

207
00:12:28,920 --> 00:12:30,140
I know you won't.

208
00:12:30,680 --> 00:12:33,200
Your vessel is a slave ship, after all.

209
00:12:33,440 --> 00:12:35,820
If you hurt me, I'll be worth less.

210
00:12:36,220 --> 00:12:39,867
I should have fled the moment I
saw your wicked-looking faces.

211
00:12:40,280 --> 00:12:41,440
How foolish of me.

212
00:12:44,700 --> 00:12:46,240
You're gonna drown, girl.

213
00:12:46,520 --> 00:12:48,167
There's nowhere left to run.

214
00:12:48,400 --> 00:12:49,620
Just give up.

215
00:12:49,900 --> 00:12:50,760
You're wrong.

216
00:12:50,940 --> 00:12:52,200
I can still escape.

217
00:12:53,020 --> 00:12:54,580
Put that big sword away.

218
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:57,077
I promise we'll treat you nice.

219
00:12:57,160 --> 00:12:59,480
You'll be our little treasure, okay?

220
00:13:00,860 --> 00:13:01,720
It's time.

221
00:13:02,040 --> 00:13:04,620
I must escape into the future once again.

222
00:13:16,900 --> 00:13:18,760
What the hell is that thing?

223
00:13:28,440 --> 00:13:30,440
I see myself!

224
00:13:33,520 --> 00:13:37,820
I heard a young woman's
voice crying out for help.

225
00:13:38,100 --> 00:13:39,040
It can speak.

226
00:13:42,820 --> 00:13:45,000
Are you all right, miss?

227
00:13:46,260 --> 00:13:48,900
You are injured, are you?

228
00:14:07,520 --> 00:14:08,880
Oh, my!

229
00:14:09,660 --> 00:14:11,880
It may hurt you.

230
00:14:12,460 --> 00:14:13,290
What?

231
00:14:13,373 --> 00:14:15,300
No, I'm just a little shaken up.

232
00:14:15,440 --> 00:14:19,440
But wait, does that mean
you came here to save me?

233
00:14:21,000 --> 00:14:22,120
I did.

234
00:14:25,200 --> 00:14:28,060
I'm so glad you're all right.

235
00:14:34,100 --> 00:14:36,280
You're in much worse shape than me.

236
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:39,460
Come on, stay with me, please.

237
00:14:45,120 --> 00:14:46,220
Odin disappeared.

238
00:14:46,800 --> 00:14:49,500
What happened? Where did he go? Damn it.

239
00:14:49,860 --> 00:14:52,272
There were only a few minutes left to go.

240
00:14:52,480 --> 00:14:56,340
He was so close to making it, but
he couldn't hold on. He's dead!

241
00:14:56,560 --> 00:14:59,097
I don't think it's fair
what you did to him, Pops!

242
00:14:59,180 --> 00:15:01,317
Yeah, he gave it his best back there!

243
00:15:01,400 --> 00:15:03,282
You should have let him join us!

244
00:15:03,420 --> 00:15:04,280
Lord Odin!

245
00:15:05,420 --> 00:15:06,340
Lord Odin!

246
00:15:07,780 --> 00:15:08,737
Hey, stop me!

247
00:15:08,820 --> 00:15:09,860
Let go of me now!

248
00:15:10,220 --> 00:15:11,160
Answer me!

249
00:15:12,620 --> 00:15:13,540
Lord Odin!

250
00:15:26,960 --> 00:15:29,140
He's recovering so fast.

251
00:15:29,420 --> 00:15:31,380
I didn't realize he was a human.

252
00:15:43,820 --> 00:15:44,660
Yes!

253
00:15:50,440 --> 00:15:51,560
Wow! Wow!

254
00:15:51,940 --> 00:15:55,077
A fierce struggle, but I still
couldn't get on Whitebeard's ship.

255
00:15:55,160 --> 00:16:00,042
All those dreams of touring around the
world just sailed right away, but no matter!

256
00:16:06,760 --> 00:16:08,240
I still did it!

257
00:16:08,440 --> 00:16:12,180
I set foot on foreign soil for
the first time ever! Finally!

258
00:16:15,340 --> 00:16:16,437
So cheery.

259
00:16:16,520 --> 00:16:18,980
My adventure has begun at last!

260
00:16:19,220 --> 00:16:21,455
The land of Wano is far behind me now!

261
00:16:21,560 --> 00:16:23,640
The world is my oyster! I'm free!

262
00:16:24,940 --> 00:16:26,680
Don't jump around so much!

263
00:16:26,880 --> 00:16:30,600
You're healing fast, but you're
not fully recovered yet! Huh?

264
00:16:31,740 --> 00:16:32,680
I see!

265
00:16:33,040 --> 00:16:35,497
So you're the woman who
nursed me back to health!

266
00:16:35,580 --> 00:16:37,180
Yes, sort of.

267
00:16:37,500 --> 00:16:38,800
Thank you very much!

268
00:16:40,140 --> 00:16:43,300
Oh no, it's the least I
could do after you saved me!

269
00:16:43,960 --> 00:16:45,717
Truly, I am in your debt, sir.

270
00:16:45,800 --> 00:16:49,388
Well, miss, we're both safe now,
and that's all that matters.

271
00:16:49,740 --> 00:16:53,564
By the way, did I hear you say
that you're from the land of Wano?

272
00:16:54,160 --> 00:16:55,440
That I am, yes.

273
00:16:56,440 --> 00:16:57,734
And speaking of which,

274
00:16:57,960 --> 00:16:59,957
I've come all the way to a foreign land,

275
00:17:00,040 --> 00:17:02,357
but you're dressed like you're
from the flower capital.

276
00:17:02,440 --> 00:17:05,616
I would have thought you'd
wear something more exotic.

277
00:17:06,540 --> 00:17:09,200
Well, the truth is, since I was a child,

278
00:17:09,340 --> 00:17:11,987
it's been my dream to
visit the land of Wano.

279
00:17:12,400 --> 00:17:16,780
When you return home, would you be
so kind as to take me along with you?

280
00:17:21,980 --> 00:17:23,020
He's annoyed.

281
00:17:28,840 --> 00:17:29,720
That's her!

282
00:17:29,980 --> 00:17:31,020
Right over there!

283
00:17:34,080 --> 00:17:36,280
We're counting on you, Captain Karma!

284
00:17:43,060 --> 00:17:45,160
Six hearts! Wow, fascinating!

285
00:17:45,700 --> 00:17:48,717
Back at home, we don't have
anybody built like that!

286
00:17:48,800 --> 00:17:49,630
Huh?

287
00:17:49,800 --> 00:17:50,630
Hey!

288
00:17:50,713 --> 00:17:54,051
I thought you guys said there
was a monster protecting her!

289
00:17:54,900 --> 00:17:57,200
Huh? That's funny! Where'd it go?

290
00:17:57,980 --> 00:18:00,820
I mean, it's way too big to hide!

291
00:18:03,200 --> 00:18:04,420
Well, you're back!

292
00:18:04,860 --> 00:18:05,860
Can't get enough.

293
00:18:06,560 --> 00:18:07,760
Then who are you?

294
00:18:08,000 --> 00:18:10,340
Don't act like you know us, bastard!

295
00:18:11,220 --> 00:18:12,050
Huh?

296
00:18:12,133 --> 00:18:14,449
Did all of you hit your
heads or something?

297
00:18:14,580 --> 00:18:18,097
Should have known a high-class lady
would have had a bodyguard with her.

298
00:18:18,180 --> 00:18:20,592
But it'll be worth the price she fetches.

299
00:18:21,240 --> 00:18:23,800
I'll kick your ass and then sell you both!

300
00:18:25,640 --> 00:18:26,660
Let's run away.

301
00:18:27,120 --> 00:18:28,708
There are too many of them.

302
00:18:30,220 --> 00:18:31,917
My first fight overseas.

303
00:18:32,000 --> 00:18:32,940
I can't wait.

304
00:18:46,700 --> 00:18:50,877
It's the White Beard Pirates—this man,

305
00:18:50,960 --> 00:18:54,617
Karma eventually became an
associate of the White Beard Pirates

306
00:18:54,700 --> 00:18:58,037
and even fought beside them
during the war in Marineford.

307
00:18:58,120 --> 00:19:00,257
Come aboard!

308
00:19:00,340 --> 00:19:01,477
Let's go.

309
00:19:01,560 --> 00:19:04,337
Huh, but I let go of the chain back there.

310
00:19:04,420 --> 00:19:05,657
What made you change your mind?

311
00:19:05,740 --> 00:19:11,957
One woman screams and you throw
your dream away—quite the softy.

312
00:19:12,040 --> 00:19:12,870
Aren't you?

313
00:19:12,953 --> 00:19:16,517
Hurry before I change my mind!

314
00:19:16,600 --> 00:19:22,277
We're setting out on an amazing adventure,

315
00:19:22,360 --> 00:19:24,377
one beyond your wildest dreams.

316
00:19:24,460 --> 00:19:25,477
Ready, little?

317
00:19:25,560 --> 00:19:26,820
ready little

318
00:19:29,440 --> 00:19:30,270
brother.

319
00:19:30,353 --> 00:19:32,197
Are you sure, Waikichi? Hm?

320
00:19:32,280 --> 00:19:33,820
Are you talking to me?

321
00:19:38,960 --> 00:19:40,740
Let's set sail!

322
00:19:51,000 --> 00:19:51,830
Odin!

323
00:19:51,913 --> 00:19:53,300
We're so glad you're alive!

324
00:19:53,500 --> 00:19:55,677
I was starting to think
we lost you to the sea.

325
00:19:55,760 --> 00:19:57,520
Yeah, what a relief.

326
00:20:00,520 --> 00:20:02,720
Glad to be here. Thank you.

327
00:20:04,400 --> 00:20:06,817
Bob's gave you a rough
time back there, huh?

328
00:20:06,900 --> 00:20:08,040
Real nasty stuff.

329
00:20:08,400 --> 00:20:09,660
What a jerk, huh?

330
00:20:12,720 --> 00:20:14,420
Hey, I heard that.

331
00:20:15,440 --> 00:20:16,560
You're alive.

332
00:20:17,100 --> 00:20:19,980
It's such a relief to see you safe, sir.

333
00:20:20,100 --> 00:20:22,600
Yes, and better than ever, my friend.

334
00:20:23,600 --> 00:20:24,780
We're here, too.

335
00:20:29,400 --> 00:20:30,280
Dog Storm!

336
00:20:30,580 --> 00:20:31,410
Cat Piper!

337
00:20:31,493 --> 00:20:33,381
Where the hell did you come from?

338
00:20:33,580 --> 00:20:36,997
We figured Yugarra would get
on the ship one way or another,

339
00:20:37,080 --> 00:20:39,557
so we snuck on and hid
before it left Wano.

340
00:20:39,640 --> 00:20:41,640
Wherever Yugarra go, we'll follow.

341
00:20:42,860 --> 00:20:43,690
Stewards!

342
00:20:43,900 --> 00:20:47,724
A while back, you said you were
going to make me pay, didn't you?

343
00:20:49,260 --> 00:20:52,142
If you want to throw me
into the sea, then do it.

344
00:21:01,240 --> 00:21:02,980
Maybe I will someday.

345
00:21:04,380 --> 00:21:05,733
Miss, what's your name?

346
00:21:06,700 --> 00:21:08,260
Oh, pleasure to meet you.

347
00:21:08,440 --> 00:21:09,270
I'm Toki.

348
00:21:09,353 --> 00:21:11,221
Thank you so much for helping me.

349
00:21:11,320 --> 00:21:15,440
So, um, if it's not a bother, could
you take me to the land of Wano?

350
00:21:18,020 --> 00:21:18,920
She's annoyed.

351
00:21:20,360 --> 00:21:22,220
I'll help out however I can.

352
00:21:22,460 --> 00:21:24,597
So please let me stay on board this ship.

353
00:21:24,680 --> 00:21:26,300
Do as you like!

354
00:21:32,620 --> 00:21:34,800
Every sight, every sound,

355
00:21:34,900 --> 00:21:39,429
and every experience that I have will
be faithfully chronicled in my journal.

356
00:21:43,800 --> 00:21:45,220
Enemy ship!

357
00:21:45,740 --> 00:21:47,540
Prepare for battle, everyone!

358
00:21:49,920 --> 00:21:51,580
Here we go!

359
00:21:54,680 --> 00:21:57,040
No! Not yet! Please!

360
00:21:58,620 --> 00:21:59,460
Why not?

361
00:22:09,880 --> 00:22:11,420
There! You see?

362
00:22:12,400 --> 00:22:14,480
I sank it! Idiot!

363
00:22:14,600 --> 00:22:16,000
That wasn't the plan!

364
00:22:16,140 --> 00:22:18,557
You don't get how pirates
work at all, do you?

365
00:22:18,640 --> 00:22:19,760
Oh, plunder!

366
00:22:20,060 --> 00:22:22,097
You gotta plunder the ship first!

367
00:22:22,180 --> 00:22:25,460
So many things I've
never experienced before.

368
00:22:28,020 --> 00:22:29,860
What is this place?

369
00:22:30,760 --> 00:22:33,400
Tall buildings of curious make.

370
00:22:33,640 --> 00:22:36,340
Bubble encased trees
undulating like jelly.

371
00:22:38,760 --> 00:22:40,220
Odin, wait!

372
00:22:40,540 --> 00:22:42,128
We don't know if it's safe!

373
00:22:45,100 --> 00:22:47,180
A world of wonders.

374
00:22:52,840 --> 00:22:54,060
No way!

375
00:22:57,220 --> 00:22:58,050
Odin!

376
00:23:00,080 --> 00:23:02,360
A chill like none other.

377
00:23:15,180 --> 00:23:17,020
A heat like none other.

378
00:23:18,080 --> 00:23:18,910
Odin!

379
00:23:19,120 --> 00:23:20,820
Hang on, I got you!

380
00:23:34,400 --> 00:23:36,720
Adventure, here I come!

381
00:23:37,900 --> 00:23:39,660
Peculiar plants.

382
00:23:44,720 --> 00:23:46,220
Come here.

383
00:23:46,500 --> 00:23:48,060
Astonishing animals.

384
00:23:50,940 --> 00:23:52,680
Humongous humans!

385
00:23:57,080 --> 00:23:58,920
Step back, kid!

386
00:24:07,040 --> 00:24:08,757
All right!

387
00:24:08,840 --> 00:24:10,100
Wa-ha-ha!

388
00:24:16,760 --> 00:24:17,590
Wa-ha-ha!

389
00:24:17,673 --> 00:24:18,937
Strength like I'd never seen!

390
00:24:19,020 --> 00:24:19,850
And courage!

391
00:24:22,800 --> 00:24:25,300
But more than that, ideas.

392
00:24:25,800 --> 00:24:28,500
Every day my eyes are opened in new ways.

393
00:24:28,660 --> 00:24:32,840
I realize how narrow my vision was
before I embarked on this journey.

394
00:24:33,080 --> 00:24:37,380
I see now that I am only a tiny
piece of a great wide world!

395
00:24:40,480 --> 00:24:41,677
How old am I?

396
00:24:41,760 --> 00:24:47,337
I'm 26, but I was born long ago,
so technically I'm 800 years old.

397
00:24:47,420 --> 00:24:51,500
So what you're saying is: you're
young but you're old as dirt.

398
00:24:55,740 --> 00:25:01,360
It seems that even leaping through time
is possible; the world is a big place.

399
00:25:02,960 --> 00:25:05,317
I have learned that this world consists of

400
00:25:05,400 --> 00:25:08,660
four large seas and one
long narrow waterway.

401
00:25:09,480 --> 00:25:12,892
And apparently the planet
itself is round like a dumpling.

402
00:25:13,720 --> 00:25:15,400
What a mysterious thing.

403
00:25:17,580 --> 00:25:18,840
What do you think?

404
00:25:19,240 --> 00:25:20,416
Enjoying the voyage?

405
00:25:20,960 --> 00:25:21,790
Certainly.

406
00:25:21,873 --> 00:25:23,100
The world is amazing.

407
00:25:23,380 --> 00:25:24,620
I want to see more.

408
00:25:24,960 --> 00:25:27,019
I'm glad to hear you're having fun.

409
00:25:27,440 --> 00:25:28,460
What is that?

410
00:25:28,720 --> 00:25:29,600
A map.

411
00:25:30,260 --> 00:25:33,800
In these vast seas, the land
of Wano is hardly a speck.

412
00:25:34,160 --> 00:25:36,820
So, which region is
your family from, Toki?

413
00:25:38,660 --> 00:25:39,600
I'm not sure.

414
00:25:40,920 --> 00:25:44,744
All I know is that both of my
parents were from the land of Wano.

415
00:25:46,220 --> 00:25:50,808
Even if that doesn't seem like much,
Wano is the only place I have left to go.

416
00:25:51,360 --> 00:25:55,125
But I'm afraid the ship won't
make it there for quite some time.

417
00:25:58,280 --> 00:25:59,460
I am sorry.

418
00:26:01,300 --> 00:26:02,130
It's fine.

419
00:26:02,380 --> 00:26:04,880
I'm rather enjoying my travels with you.

420
00:26:05,840 --> 00:26:10,546
Because when you and I are together, I
feel like I'm exactly where I need to be.

421
00:26:11,600 --> 00:26:12,600
Why is that?

422
00:26:13,500 --> 00:26:14,500
I wonder.

423
00:26:15,280 --> 00:26:17,220
How peculiar. A mystery.

424
00:26:22,480 --> 00:26:23,380
Hey, guys.

425
00:26:23,960 --> 00:26:25,666
Where'd Lord Oden run off to?

426
00:26:26,180 --> 00:26:27,080
Oh, there.

427
00:26:28,000 --> 00:26:29,340
Don't bother them.

428
00:26:43,260 --> 00:26:45,960
I soon learned that
Whitebeard has an enemy.

429
00:26:46,300 --> 00:26:48,420
The Navy's here. Let's retreat.

430
00:26:50,400 --> 00:26:51,640
Why did we flee?

431
00:26:51,980 --> 00:26:53,897
They look like a worthy challenge.

432
00:26:53,980 --> 00:26:55,477
We should have fought them.

433
00:26:55,560 --> 00:26:57,300
You don't know the Navy, huh?

434
00:26:58,320 --> 00:26:59,880
It's a big organization.

435
00:27:00,340 --> 00:27:05,140
Even if we take them down today, more
and more ships will come after us. Hm?

436
00:27:05,640 --> 00:27:09,169
Wow, so there's a group that
controls the entire world, huh?

437
00:27:09,820 --> 00:27:11,780
A mighty adversary, indeed!

438
00:27:12,420 --> 00:27:14,497
Yeah, wait till you've traveled some more.

439
00:27:14,580 --> 00:27:16,933
Then you can decide how mighty they are.

440
00:27:17,380 --> 00:27:20,220
Your country's still free, after all.

441
00:27:20,960 --> 00:27:21,790
Oh?

442
00:27:28,520 --> 00:27:30,814
Ah, nothing in the paper today, either.

443
00:27:31,460 --> 00:27:32,290
What?!

444
00:27:32,373 --> 00:27:33,977
Another story on Whitebeard?!

445
00:27:34,060 --> 00:27:35,825
But we're causing trouble too!

446
00:27:36,220 --> 00:27:37,985
Hey, I'm still reading, dummy.

447
00:27:38,300 --> 00:27:41,377
Anyway, Whitebeard has that
Wano samurai on his crew.

448
00:27:41,460 --> 00:27:44,578
Seems like that guy's doing
crazy stuff all the time.

449
00:27:46,360 --> 00:27:47,380
Hey, Captain.

450
00:27:50,920 --> 00:27:54,400
A samurai from a land
shield away from the world.

451
00:27:55,360 --> 00:27:57,560
Sure hope I get to meet him someday.

452
00:28:04,060 --> 00:28:06,120
Thank you.
